  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-02-04T16:53:06.844Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This has been an issue for a couple years now.\n\nWhen applying eyelid bone rotations for eye-tracking instead of the usual blendshapes, I can set it up in Unity and everything seems to work like how it does with blendshapes. However, once it uploads to vrchat, the eyelids never use the \"looking down,\" \"looking up\" rotation states, and the blinking is only about 2 frames of instant blink. There are no in-between frames with blinking and it's jarring and unnatural.\n\nWhat I don't understand is why the SDK allows us to adjust these settings and test them in the Untiy inspector without ever actually using them in-game.\n\nA lot of my models require rotations for eyelids instead of blendshapes because they eyeballs are convex and the eyelids would clip through the eyeballs when using blendshapes. \n\nI would be fine with making a blinking animation, but doing so doesn't let me use the \"looking up \" and \"looking down\" features that the SDK can do. \n\nPlease fix this.",
